<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="overview"><h2>Overview</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<p>Developed as part of GadJet&#39;s Product Design and Graphics team, the Display Visualiser gives B2B customers an interactive way to inspect retail stands online and preview their main dimensions at life size in their own store before ordering.</p>
<p>It combines a straightforward model-viewer experience with a repeatable process for producing highly optimised web and AR assets.</p>
<section class="case-scan-stats" aria-label="Display Visualiser project scale">
  <div><strong>11</strong><span>AR-ready retail displays</span></div>
  <div><strong>2</strong><span>brands</span></div>
  <div><strong>3</strong><span>live B2B catalogue surfaces</span></div>
</section>
<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="the-problem"><h2>The problem</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<p>B2B customers previously had to judge a display from product dimensions and static photographs. These communicate its appearance, but not how it will occupy a real retail environment. This is particularly important across compact counter displays, modular units and larger floor-standing displays, where footprint, height, visibility and surrounding space influence the purchasing decision.</p>
<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="the-solution"><h2>The solution</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<p>Each display can be rotated and examined in the browser, then placed through mobile AR at life size. This gives retailers a clearer way to assess a stand’s main height, visual presence and general placement before committing to it.</p>
<figure class="case-media case-transparent is-wide"><img src="../../media/projects/gadjet-displays/case-study/display-range.AVIF" alt="A range of optimised GadJet and Goodiz retail-display models" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="building-the-display-models"><h2>Building the display models</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<p>Eleven retail displays were prepared for the experience: five GadJet stands and six Goodiz stands. Each was recreated as a dedicated 3D asset, preserving the main display dimensions, stocked products and branding. Rear support structures were omitted to keep the presentation clean, rather than reproducing every construction detail.</p>
<p>The main display dimensions were kept at real-world scale for AR placement. As the models omit rear supports, they do not represent the complete installed footprint. They help customers assess appearance and general placement; installation clearances should be checked against the full physical stand specifications.</p>
<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="optimising-for-the-web"><h2>Optimising for the web</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<p>Most web models are under 1 MB. Texture use was kept deliberately low and lower-resolution WebP maps reduced delivered file size without losing the key product and brand details.</p>
<div class="case-stat-callout">
  <strong>&lt;1 MB</strong>
  <span>Most web 3D models</span>
</div>
<p>Repeated products and structural components were linked within each model, so stocked stands could reuse geometry instead of storing the same object repeatedly.</p>
<p>Separate Android and iOS AR assets retain clearer detail at close range. Their texture formats and material properties were tuned for each platform so finishes remain convincing across the web viewer, Android and iOS.</p>
<p>Ray-traced lighting was baked into each asset, preserving consistent light, shadow and material definition without requiring real-time ray tracing on the customer&#39;s device.</p>
<ol class="case-process-strip" aria-label="3D optimisation workflow">
  <li>Linked geometry</li>
  <li>Optimised textures</li>
  <li>Baked lighting</li>
  <li>Platform-specific AR</li>
</ol>
<p>Together, these decisions keep detailed displays practical across desktop and mobile hardware while allowing the AR versions to withstand closer inspection.</p>
<div class="section-heading case-section-heading" id="interactive-3d-viewer"><h2>Interactive 3D viewer</h2><span aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../projects/gadjet-displays/stand-viewer.css">
<script src="../../projects/gadjet-displays/stand-viewer.js" defer></script>
